1
00:00:04,337 --> 00:00:06,047
(Leonard:)Hmm.

2
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:08,129
(Sheldon:)The problem appears to be unsolvable.

3
00:00:08,299 --> 00:00:10,389
Maybe we could run
some computer simulations.

4
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,802
There are many variables.
It would take forever.

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:15,181
We've gotta be missing something.

6
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:16,598
Okay. Let's start again.

7
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:20,226
The movie is playing here at 7:20,
here at 7:40...

8
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:22,645
...here at 8: 10, and here at 8:45.

9
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:25,693
(Penny:)All right.
These theaters have to be eliminated.

10
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:29,319
Why? They're state of the art:
digital projection, surround sound.

11
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:32,157
(Sheldon:)Yes, but they have no Icee machines.

12
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:36,079
(Sheldon:)Despite my aggressive
letter-writing campaign, I might add.

13
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:39,666
(Raj:)What about the multiplex here?
The seats are terrific.

14
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:44,581
(Sheldon:)They have Twizzlers instead of Red Vines.
No lumbar support can compensate for that.

15
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:49,297
It's gonna take an hour to eat and I don't
see a Sheldon-approved restaurant...

16
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,886
(Leonard:)...proximate
to a Sheldon-approved theater.

17
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,552
- We could eat after the movie.
- Unacceptable.

18
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:58,221
(Sheldon:)The delay would result in tomorrow
morning's bowel movement at work.

19
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:02,566
(Raj:)Hang on, hang on.
There's a 7-Eleven here.

